<title>BELGIUM: Belgian yr/yr inflation 1.74 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Belgian yr/yr inflation 1.74 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economics Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES     June	 May	  June 1996</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 124.30     124.09     122.17</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.17	 0.15	 0.01</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   1.74	 1.58	 1.80</p>
<p>NOTE - forecast for June CPI 1.7 percent.  </p>
<p>    Health index *		  121.67     121.45</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.18	 0.10</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for fresh friut, meats, foreign travel, and restaurant and cafe bills, while for potatoes lower prices were recorded.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
